8.2 Fargate Pricing Model
Fargate is billed based on the vCPU and memory resources allocated to the task, for the duration from task start to task stop. There are no minimum charges, no reserved capacity costs, and no idle billing.
	∙	A task configured with 1 vCPU and 2GB memory running for 10 minutes costs approximately $0.02–$0.04 USD per execution.
	∙	A task configured with 2 vCPU and 4GB memory running for 20 minutes costs approximately $0.08–$0.12 USD per execution.
	∙	Contrast this with an m5.large EC2 instance (~$0.096/hour) running 24/7 regardless of task activity — over $69/month per instance before any operational cost.
8.3 Cost Optimisation Opportunities
	∙	Right-size each tenant’s task definition independently — no need to size for the largest tenant across the fleet.
	∙	Use Fargate Spot for non-critical or development DBT runs to reduce execution cost by up to 70%.
	∙	Implement per-tenant cost tagging to enable accurate chargeback and cost attribution in multi-tenant billing models.
	∙	Add VPC endpoints for ECR and S3 to eliminate NAT Gateway data transfer costs.
	∙	Schedule non-urgent DBT runs during off-peak hours to benefit from Fargate Spot availability windows.

